.TH TFF 1 "September 2026" "TFF 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tff, tff2, tff_linux \- Ten Flying Fingers keyboard remapping daemon and chord engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tff
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B tff
\fBmonitor\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIDEVICE\fR]
.br
.B tff
\fBcheatsheet\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICONFIG_FILE\fR]
.br
.B tff
\fBvalidate\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICONFIG_FILE\fR]
.br
.B tff
\fBsetup\-udev\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBTen Flying Fingers (TFF)\fR is a high-performance, low-latency keyboard remapper and chording engine implemented in C++. It allows overlapping key combinations (chords) to trigger complex keystrokes, navigation commands, modal layers, and mouse movements.
.PP
The engine supports:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOverlapping Combos & Chords\fR: Order-independent or order-dependent combinations (e.g. \fBJ+F\fR for Backspace, \fBF+J\fR for Delete, \fBD+F+J\fR for Escape).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDual-Role Tap-Hold Keys\fR: Keys that emit one key on short tap (e.g. CapsLock \(-> Escape) and a modifier or layer on hold (CapsLock held \(-> Super / Win).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBModal & Toggle Layers\fR: Switch full keyboard layouts while holding a key or toggle them on and off (e.g. navigation, numeric keypad, symbols).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSequential Leader Sequences\fR: Vim-like sequence leader keys (Leader \(-> w \(-> q \(-> Save & Quit).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAuto-Shift\fR: Tap a key for lowercase, hold briefly for uppercase, eliminating the need for the physical Shift key.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBHome-Row Mouse Keys\fR: Move pointer, click, drag, and scroll directly from the keyboard without reaching for a physical mouse.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BR monitor " [" \fIOPTIONS\fR "] [" \fIDEVICE\fR "]"
Launch the interactive live event monitor and chord debugger. Displays microsecond timestamps, timing deltas, raw key codes, chord candidate matching, and action annotations in real time. Runs non-exclusively by default so normal keyboard usage is unaffected.
.TP
.BR cheatsheet " [" \fIOPTIONS\fR "] [" \fICONFIG_FILE\fR "]"
Display a formatted terminal table or markdown document summarizing all active key combinations, tap-hold dual-role keys, layers, leader sequences, auto-shift keys, and settings.
.TP
.BR validate " [" \fIOPTIONS\fR "] [" \fICONFIG_FILE\fR "]"
Parse and validate a YAML configuration file without capturing input or creating virtual devices. Returns exit status 0 if valid, non-zero on error.
.TP
.BR setup\-udev " [" \fIOPTIONS\fR "]"
Inspect system permissions for non-root execution (access to \fI/dev/uinput\fR and \fI/dev/input/event*\fR), report diagnostic status, or generate/install standard udev rules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Path to YAML combo configuration file (default: \fIconfig/tff-combos.yaml\fR).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch\-config
Watch configuration file for live changes via \fBinotify\fR and automatically reload combos.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-device " \fIPATH\fR"
Attach directly to a specific input device (e.g. \fI/dev/input/event3\fR). Can be specified multiple times. If omitted, all detected physical keyboards are opened.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-grab
Acquire an exclusive grab (\fBEVIOCGRAB\fR) on input keyboards so raw keypresses are suppressed from the host OS. (Default behavior in daemon mode).
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-grab
Disable exclusive device grab. Raw events are mirrored to the host OS in addition to remapped virtual events.
.TP
.BR \-\-hotplug
Enable dynamic device hotplugging via \fBinotify\fR (default). Automatically attaches newly plugged keyboards and detaches unplugged keyboards without daemon restart.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-hotplug
Disable dynamic inotify hotplugging.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List all auto-discovered keyboard devices and persistent \fIby-id\fR symlinks, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging of intercepted and emitted events to stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-plain ", " \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colors and formatting in terminal output.
.TP
.BR \-\-markdown ", " \-\-md
Output tables in GitHub-flavored Markdown (used with \fBcheatsheet\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-deltas
Disable timing delta displays in live event monitor.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-emitted
Disable emitted virtual key lines in live event monitor.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-install
Install udev rules to \fI/etc/udev/rules.d/\fR and trigger \fBudevadm\fR reload (used with \fBsetup\-udev\fR; requires root or sudo).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print
Print recommended udev rules to stdout without modifying system files (used with \fBsetup\-udev\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-check
Check user permissions and device status (default action for \fBsetup\-udev\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-rule\-path " \fIPATH\fR"
Custom destination path for udev rules file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command usage and options, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display program version information, then exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tff/tff-combos.yaml
System-wide configuration file (used by systemd service).
.TP
.I ~/.config/tff/tff-combos.yaml
Per-user configuration file (used by user systemd service).
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/99-tff.rules
Udev rule granting non-root read/write access to \fI/dev/uinput\fR and \fI/dev/input/event*\fR.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/ten-flying-fingers.service
Systemd background service definition.
.TP
.I /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/tff
Bash shell autocompletion script.
.TP
.I /usr/share/zsh/site-functions/_tff
Zsh shell autocompletion script.
.TP
.I /usr/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/tff.fish
Fish shell autocompletion script.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set (regardless of value), disables ANSI color escape sequences across all subcommands.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run the live chord monitor to debug chord timings:
.RS 4
.B tff monitor
.RE
.PP
Inspect active key combinations in markdown format:
.RS 4
.B tff cheatsheet --markdown
.RE
.PP
Verify and install udev rules for non-root execution:
.RS 4
.B sudo tff setup\-udev --install
.RE
.PP
Validate custom combo configuration:
.RS 4
.B tff validate config/tff-combos.yaml
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR evtest (1),
.BR systemd (1),
.BR udev (7)
.PP
Configuration recipes, troubleshooting, and architecture documentation are available online at:
.RS 4
.I https://github.com/guettli/tff2/tree/main/docs
.RE
